{
    "background_story": "In ancient Greek mythology, Atreus was a king of Mycenae, known for his cunning and cleverness. However, his claim to fame was being a counterperson to the great hero, Hercules. While Hercules was on a quest to complete his twelve labors, Atreus often found ways to thwart his progress, testing the hero's resolve and ingenuity. Atreus would secretly manipulate events, creating obstacles and challenges for Hercules to overcome. Despite his mischievous nature, Atreus was not inherently evil; he simply believed that true greatness could only be achieved by facing adversity. His actions pushed Hercules to become an even greater hero, earning Atreus a place in the annals of mythological history as a counterperson who brought out the best in others.",
